@startuml
title Patrón DAO / Repository mediante Spring Data JPA
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontColor #123B52
skinparam ArrowColor #1E5A78
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #E9F3F7
skinparam participantBorderColor #1E5A78
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

participant "AppointmentController\nHTTP y DTO" as Controller
participant "AppointmentService\nnegocio y @Transactional" as Service
participant "AppointmentRepository\ninterface JpaRepository" as Repository
participant "Spring Data JPA\nHibernate ORM" as ORM
database "PostgreSQL 16\npersistencia" as DB

Controller -> Service : findAppointments()
Service -> Repository : findAllByPatientIdOrderByCreatedAtDesc(patientId)
Repository -> ORM : consulta derivada de Spring Data
ORM -> DB : JDBC / SQL
DB --> ORM : filas
ORM --> Repository : entidades Appointment
Repository --> Service : List<Appointment>
Service --> Controller : List<AppointmentResponseDTO>

note over Repository
  Otros ejemplos reales: PatientRepository,
  AvailabilitySlotRepository y UserRepository.
end note
note over Repository, ORM
  Repository cumple la responsabilidad de acceso
  a datos equivalente al patrón DAO.
end note
@enduml
